WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.220
Lemonate's 50% fsd discount in Tennessee shows insurers beginning to separate supervised autonomy

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:14.000
miles from human driving and real pricing. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 562. Lemonade

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:20.640
now offers the program in Tennessee and halves the per mile rate when fsd is active. The insurer

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:27.420
pulls data directly from Tesla's fleet API to distinguish human and supervised miles. Vehicles

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:33.420
need hardware 4 or newer with compatible firmware. The change lowers ownership costs while giving

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:40.940
lemonade more granular risk data. Because fsd remains a level 2 supervised system, drivers must stay

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:47.020
attentive even when the discount applies. Insurance pricing for supervised autonomy is shifting from

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:53.520
blanket risk pools to mile-by-mile separation of human and machine driving. Lemonade's Tennessee

00:00:53.520 --> 00:01:01.320
program pulls real-time data from Tesla's fleet API to apply a 50% discount only on fsd miles,

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:07.220
creating a measurable price signal that owners can see on every statement. This matters because

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:13.880
it turns a regulatory classification, level 2 supervision, into an economic variable that directly

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:20.620
affects total cost of ownership. The discount applies automatically whenever the car is under fsd

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:26.400
control, giving drivers an immediate financial incentive to engage the system more often.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:32.600
The approach differs from traditional auto insurance, which spreads risk across all drivers and

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:38.140
vehicle types. By tying the discount to hardware generation and firmware compatibility,

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:44.340
lemonade is effectively pricing the incremental safety or predictability that the system delivers

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:51.100
today, not the future unsupervised promise. If the data shows lower claim frequency on those

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:57.560
miles, the model becomes self-reinforcing. If claims remain flat, the discount shrinks or disappears.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:03.900
The requirement for hardware 4 or newer also creates a de facto hardware upgrade pressure

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:10.180
for owners seeking the lowest rates. For Tesla, the implication is straightforward. Lower effective

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:15.600
ownership costs can accelerate fsd adoption, even while the system stays supervised.

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:21.500
The same preference data lemonade is now pricing is exactly what Tesla is studying internally.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:28.580
Tesla is examining driver disengagement to identify preference-based exits rather than safety issues.

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:35.040
The effort covers navigation choices as well. This approach could reduce unnecessary interventions

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:41.300
and improve perceived smoothness. The work builds on earlier observations that most disengagement

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:47.640
stem from driver preference rather than hazard avoidance. Next, watch how preference data feeds

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:54.160
into future software versions. Tesla states that fsd supervised can monitor multiple directions

00:02:54.160 --> 00:03:00.480
simultaneously, where a human driver cannot. The post highlights the system's ability to maintain

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:06.700
awareness across the full field at once. This capability stems from the vehicle's array of cameras

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:11.640
and real-time processing that does not suffer from single-point visual attention limits.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:18.080
The comparison underscores why Tesla positions the supervised system as already exceeding human

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:24.540
perceptual reach in certain scenarios. Samsung, Electro Mechanics, and LG Inotech secured sole

